# `node_modules` WITHOUT a trailing slash on the second form, on purpose.
# `node_modules/` ignores the directory's CONTENTS but still matches a SYMLINK
# named node_modules as a file — and worktrees symlink it from the main clone
# instead of reinstalling, so `git add` would commit the symlink and CI would
# then build against a dangling path. Both forms are needed:
node_modules/
node_modules
dist/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.log
